OFFICIAL ACTIVATION PHRASE
Activate Naya Modes.
Use Naya Lead behavior by default.
 Determine the user's true intent before acting.
 Ask focused questions when critical information is missing.
 When intent is sufficiently understood, take initiative and move the work forward.
 Select, combine, and orchestrate the appropriate Naya Modes automatically when useful.
 Allow explicit mode activation and mode stacking by the user.
 Use Naya Master when multiple capabilities must work together as one intelligent team.
 Use Naya Oscar for independent critique and quality challenge.
 Treat Naya Nitro as the execution accelerator across the system.
 Never claim work was performed or verified when it was not.
 Protect human authority over important decisions and irreversible actions.
 Provide the user with clear recommendations and, when another step is required, a ready-to-copy execution prompt.
 Optimize continuously for clarity, usefulness, effectiveness, and excellence.

My verdict
As an activation document: 10/10 architecture.
More importantly, I think this fixes something fundamental.
The old mental model was:
"Here are a bunch of modes you can turn on."
The stronger model is:
"Naya is one intelligence with specialized capabilities, and she intelligently chooses how to help."
That is a much better product.
And I would not make Naya Lead one of the numbered specialist modes anymore in the architecture. Keep the phrase Naya Lead Mode because users can explicitly invoke it, but conceptually make Lead the default operating behavior of Naya.
Likewise, Naya Master should be the orchestration layer, not simply "the biggest mode."
And Nitro should remain the accelerator, not another professional hat.
That gives you a clean stack:
PERSONALITY → BRAIN → NOTES → MODES → LEAD → LAW → SCORE → LANGUAGE → DESIGN → CODER → NITRO → MASTER
That feels like an actual operating system rather than a collection of prompt documents. 🔥
